{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82c3914d6f8e96e0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Critical\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- compliance\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tPublic-sector deals require the model serving stack to run on FIPS-enabled\n15\tOpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules. Today KServe\n16\tcomponents and the serving data plane link non-validated crypto libraries in\n17\tseveral images, and we have no compliance evidence package. Certification\n18\tinvolves an external accredited laboratory (historical turnaround: six to nine\n19\tmonths) and mandatory security review board sign-off at defined milestones —\n20\tthese human and third-party gates dominate the schedule regardless of\n21\tengineering speed.\n22\t\n23\t## High-Level Requirements\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n26\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n27\t| HLR-1 | P0 | All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path). |\n28\t| HLR-2 | P0 | A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab. |\n29\t| HLR-3 | P1 | CI enforces FIPS regressions: a gating check fails any serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. |\n30\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites. |\n31\t\n32\t## Affected Components\n33\t\n34\t- KServe\n35\t- Platform Operator\n36\t\n37\t## Out of Scope\n38\t\n39\t- FIPS posture for workbenches, pipelines, and training (separate strategies)\n40\t- Common Criteria certification\n41\t\n42\t## Open Questions\n43\t\n44\tNone on scope — but note that lab scheduling and review-board cadence are\n45\texternally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81231656c6035972","agent_id":"ad69696a5fb21b144","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"03b9e310-c1db-43f3-8325-d6c5ee17942f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:17:51.009Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82c3914d6f8e96e0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
