{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e1a591a3-5de8-45ed-9e81-0e3aa4c65227","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83b2adc02820352a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-nqv96ufk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for KServe component images\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes every KServe component image in the model serving stack run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the request path. It covers the audit, remediation, and verification of the KServe control-plane images, the FIPS regression gate for those images, and the evidence inputs (module inventory, build attestations, test results) for the KServe portion of the compliance evidence package.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all KServe component images for cryptographic library usage, producing a per-image module inventory that classifies each linked crypto library as validated or non-validated and identifies request-path usage.\n- Remediate every KServe image so that the request path uses only validated cryptographic modules on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters (rebuilds, library replacements, or base-image changes as the audit dictates — the remediation mechanism per image is an implementation decision for the team).\n- Verify correct serving behavior (inference request path) for the remediated images on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n- Author and verify the FIPS regression gating CI check covering the KServe images: a gating check that fails any KServe build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. This epic owns the portion of the stack-wide FIPS regression enforcement (HLR-3) that covers the KServe surface.\n- Produce build attestations for every remediated KServe image and hand off the per-image module inventory, attestations, and FIPS test results as inputs to the compliance evidence package.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A module inventory exists for every KServe component image, classifying each linked cryptographic library as validated or non-validated and recording request-path usage.\n- Every remediated KServe image runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with no non-validated crypto in the inference request path, demonstrated by test results captured per image.\n- The FIPS regression gating check fails a KServe build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes a clean build (verified with a deliberate negative test), and it is wired as a gating check in the KServe build pipeline.\n- Build attestations are produced for every remediated KServe image and are available to the compliance evidence package.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — KServe portion: all KServe component images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules.\n- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — this epic authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check covering the KServe images it remediates; the check spans exactly the same images and build pipeline as the remediation, so it is not separately schedulable from this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P0, partial input)** — produces the KServe module inventory, build attestations, and test results consumed by the compliance evidence package.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43363,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81231656c6035972","agent_id":"ad69696a5fb21b144","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"a69429c4-2fd8-423c-90e0-ec84dc9d04db","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:22:01.327Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
