me surface.\n- Produce build attestations for every remediated data-plane image and hand off the per-image module inventory, attestations, and FIPS test results as inputs to the compliance evidence package.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A module inventory exists for every serving-runtime data-plane image, classifying each linked cryptographic library as validated or non-validated and recording request-path usage.\n- Every remediated data-plane image runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with no non-validated crypto in the inference request path, demonstrated by test results captured per image.\n- The FIPS regression gating check fails a serving-runtime build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes a clean build (verified with a deliberate negative test), and it is wired as a gating check in the serving-runtime build pipelines.\n- Build attestations are produced for every remediated data-plane image and are available to the compliance evidence package.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — serving data-plane portion (\"all serving-stack images\"): the model-execution runtime images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules.\n- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — this epic authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check covering the data-plane images it remediates; the check spans exactly the same images and build pipelines as the remediation, so it is not separately schedulable from this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P0, partial input)** — produces the data-plane module inventory, build attestations, and test results consumed by the compliance evidence package.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44210,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81231656c6035972","agent_id":"ad69696a5fb21b144","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"81f0bed8-a68b-4e76-a696-29b3d7b5779a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:2