nce package.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The Platform Operator has no architecture-context file in `.context/architecture-context/`; its build and attestation pipeline posture could not be corroborated during decomposition. Confirm the operator's build pipeline can produce the attestations the evidence package requires before scheduling.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A module inventory exists for the Platform Operator image, classifying each linked cryptographic library as validated or non-validated and recording request-path usage.\n- The remediated Platform Operator image runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with no non-validated crypto in the request path, demonstrated by captured test results.\n- The FIPS regression gating check fails a Platform Operator build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes a clean build (verified with a deliberate negative test), and it is wired as a gating check in the operator's build pipeline.\n- Build attestations are produced for the remediated operator image and are available to the compliance evidence package.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — Platform Operator portion (\"all serving-stack images\"): the operator image runs correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules.\n- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — this epic authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check covering the Platform Operator image it remediates; the check spans exactly the same image and build pipeline as the remediation, so it is not separately schedulable from this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P0, partial input)** — produces the operator module inventory, build attestations, and test results consumed by the compliance evidence package.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45041,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81231656c6035972","agent_id":"ad69696a5fb21b144","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b