{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-85351137-bebb-4947-8537-41234fe467e6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a549e0450df80292","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-nqv96ufk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E004.md","content":"# Compliance evidence package assembly and certification submission\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results covering every serving-stack image — and submits it through the security review board to the external accredited certification laboratory. It runs after the serving-stack image remediation work (KServe control plane, serving-runtime data plane, and Platform Operator) has produced its per-surface inventories, attestations, and test results.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the evidence package structure: the module inventory, build attestations, and FIPS test results required per serving-stack image, in the format the security review board and certification lab accept.\n- Aggregate and reconcile the per-surface module inventories, build attestations, and test results produced by the image remediation work into a single, internally consistent package covering every serving-stack image.\n- Run the package through the mandatory security review board sign-off at the defined milestones, incorporating required corrections.\n- Submit the approved package to the external accredited certification laboratory and drive the submission through triage.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The accredited laboratory's turnaround is historically six to nine months, and the security review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. Certification completion is therefore a schedule risk on this epic, not an acceptance criterion — the acceptance criteria below sit on the deliverable and submission, which the engineering work controls.\n- Workbenches, pipelines, and training FIPS posture, and Common Criteria certification, are out of scope for this strategy and excluded from the package.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The evidence package contains a module inventory, build attestations, and FIPS test results for every serving-stack image (KServe control plane, serving-runtime data plane, Platform Operator), with no gaps or unresolved contradictions between per-surface inputs.\n- The evidence package passes the security review board sign-off required at the defined milestones.\n- The evidence package is submitted to the external accredited certification laboratory and the submission is accepted for triage.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — this epic assembles the compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) and submits it through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45869,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81231656c6035972","agent_id":"ad69696a5fb21b144","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"7fce4799-b711-4ec1-b641-10b280c3e2ca","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:22:27.922Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
