{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be6433a9646af70d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for KServe component images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for KServe component images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes every KServe component image in the model serving stack run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the request path. It covers the audit, remediation, and verification of the KServe control-plane images, the FIPS regression gate for those images, and the evidence inputs (module inventory, build attestations, test results) for the KServe portion of the compliance evidence package.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit all KServe component images for cryptographic library usage, producing a per-image module inventory that classifies each linked crypto library as validated or non-validated and identifies request-path usage.\n38\t- Remediate every KServe image so that the request path uses only validated cryptographic modules on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters (rebuilds, library replacements, or base-image changes as the audit dictates — the remediation mechanism per image is an implementation decision for the team).\n39\t- Verify correct serving behavior (inference request path) for the remediated images on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n40\t- Author and verify the FIPS regression gating CI check covering the KServe images: a gating check that fails any KServe build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. This epic owns the portion of the stack-wide FIPS regression enforcement (HLR-3) that covers the KServe surface.\n41\t- Produce build attestations for every remediated KServe image and hand off the per-image module inventory, attestations, and FIPS test results as inputs to the compliance evidence package.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A module inventory exists for every KServe component image, classifying each linked cryptographic library as validated or non-validated and recording request-path usage.\n46\t- Every remediated KServe image runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with no non-validated crypto in the inference request path, demonstrated by test results captured per image.\n47\t- The FIPS regression gating check fails a KServe build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes a clean build (verified with a deliberate negative test), and it is wired as a gating check in the KServe build pipeline.\n48\t- Build attestations are produced for every remediated KServe image and are available to the compliance evidence package.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — KServe portion: all KServe component images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules.\n53\t- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — this epic authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check covering the KServe images it remediates; the check spans exactly the same images and build pipeline as the remediation, so it is not separately schedulable from this epic.\n54\t- **HLR-2 (P0, partial input)** — produces the KServe module inventory, build attestations, and test results consumed by the compliance evidence package.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b541f3c1e68683f5","agent_id":"ada89111e39959723","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"89e32bb9-f915-4cf3-b673-30b1caa57ad6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:24:16.316Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be6433a9646af70d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
