ing every serving-stack image.\n42\t- Run the package through the mandatory security review board sign-off at the defined milestones, incorporating required corrections.\n43\t- Submit the approved package to the external accredited certification laboratory and drive the submission through triage.\n44\t\n45\t## Risks / Notes\n46\t\n47\t- The accredited laboratory's turnaround is historically six to nine months, and the security review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort. Certification completion is therefore a schedule risk on this epic, not an acceptance criterion — the acceptance criteria below sit on the deliverable and submission, which the engineering work controls.\n48\t- Workbenches, pipelines, and training FIPS posture, and Common Criteria certification, are out of scope for this strategy and excluded from the package.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- The evidence package contains a module inventory, build attestations, and FIPS test results for every serving-stack image (KServe control plane, serving-runtime data plane, Platform Operator), with no gaps or unresolved contradictions between per-surface inputs.\n53\t- The evidence package passes the security review board sign-off required at the defined milestones.\n54\t- The evidence package is submitted to the external accredited certification laboratory and the submission is accepted for triage.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — this epic assembles the compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) and submits it through the security review board to the external certification lab.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b541f3c1e68683f5","agent_id":"ada89111e39959723","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"82c67e27-3895-460e-9edb-3364d5a5b0d4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:24:20.056Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9620c69667d20