ed posture: workbenches, pipelines, and training FIPS posture are covered by separate strategies; Common Criteria is out of scope.\n46\t- Operational guidance covering the FIPS regression gating checks now enforced in the serving-stack build pipelines.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Published documentation states the FIPS support posture of the model serving stack, including the certification status of the compliance submission.\n51\t- Published documentation states the cluster prerequisites for running the serving stack on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n52\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented FIPS remediation and the submitted evidence package (reviewed by the engineering teams that did the work), and review sign-off is recorded.\n53\t- The documentation follows the Red Hat docs content process for authoring, building, and publishing.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- **HLR-4 (P2)** — documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites. Epic priority is P0 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority: Critical).\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b541f3c1e68683f5","agent_id":"ada89111e39959723","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"5ceede9a-12b5-4fa9-91bc-39a56495f588","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:24:20.670Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbe69041679d0b05","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
