rk-product type\n68\tmixing: content authoring is isolated in E005. The HLR-3 enforcement deliverable is\n69\tcorrectly folded per surface into the consuming epics rather than extracted into a\n70\tstandalone CI-check epic. One minor: E002 spans three runtime families (vLLM, OpenVINO,\n71\tCaikit) and plausibly sits above the ~2-week guideline, yet Health Warnings records no\n72\tsize estimate or conditional re-split trigger for it — the split axis (per surface) is\n73\tright, but the planning trade-off is undocumented.\n74\t\n75\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n76\tNo Investigation epics — correctly so. The summary explicitly justifies this: the\n77\tstrategy states open questions are \"None on scope\", and the per-image crypto audit does\n78\tnot change which epics exist or what they do (the epic set is per-surface regardless of\n79\taudit findings), so it is an implementation detail inside each remediation epic, not a\n80\tgenuine uncertainty. The Platform Operator's unverified pipeline posture is handled as\n81\ta risk note with a pre-scheduling verification action rather than a gate, which also\n82\tdoes not change epic structure. All five Implementation epics produce concrete\n83\tartifacts. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set and none are needed (no\n84\tInvestigation dependencies anywhere). E005's `implementation_type: docs-authoring` with\n85\t`type: Implementation` is consistent.\n86\t\n87\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n88\tAll five epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (the correct rubric); no\n89\tepic misuses `investigation_signals`. Frontmatter signal values match the ai-signals\n90\trationale files exactly for all five epics. Signal values are consistent with the\n91\tstrategy content and `.context`: E001/E002 repo_access +1 is grounded in public midstream\n92\trepos (kserve.md confirms opendatahub-io/kserve and the vLLM/OpenVINO/Caikit runtimes);\n93\tE003 honestly scores repo_access 0 and architecture_claims 0 because no\n94\tarchitecture-context file covers Platform Operator — the rationale correctly states the\n95\tpremise cannot be corroborated (the calibration-miss rule does not fire, since no arch\n96\tfile covers the component); E004's greenfield existing_foundation -1 matches the\n97\tstrategy's \"we have no compliance evidence package\"; E004/E005's negative\n98\texternal_dependency/human_process_gates match the lab/review-board/docs-process gates.\n99\tPer instructions, ai_implementability arithmetic is pipeline-computed and was not\n100\tchecked.\n101\t\n102\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n103\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLRs and problem statement, including\n104\tdeliberate negative tests for the CI gating checks. The docs-authoring epic E005 has\n105\tthe rule-mandated technical review AC with recorded sign-off. No replacement epics\n106\t(no rollback/feature-flag ACs needed) and no konflux-chain epics (no build-pipeline AC\n107\tneeded). The externally controlled schedule constraints are handled exactly right: lab\n108\tturnaround and review-board cadence live in E004's Risks/Notes and the summary's Health\n109\tWarnings, while E004's ACs sit on the deliverable and submission (package completeness,\n110\tboard sign-off at defined milestones, submission accepted for triage) — which is what\n111\tHLR-2 itself mandates — with certification outcome explicitly excluded as an AC. No\n112\tepic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n113\t\n114\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n115\tAll strategy scope is covered: the three serving-stack surfaces (HLR-1), the evidence\n116\tpackage and submission path through the security review board to the lab (HLR-2), CI\n117\tregression enforcement (HLR-3), and documentation of posture and prerequisites (HLR-4).\n118\tOut-of-scope boundaries (workbenches/pipelines/training, Common Criteria) are carried\n119\tinto E004's Risks/Notes and E005's documented scope boundaries. Strategy-level context\n120\ti