{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-895919f770e60d9b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for serving-runtime data-plane images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 crypto remediation for serving-runtime data-plane images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes the serving data-plane images — the model-execution runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit) that serve inference requests — run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the request path. It covers the audit, remediation, and verification of the data-plane images, the FIPS regression gate for those images, and the evidence inputs (module inventory, build attestations, test results) for the data-plane portion of the compliance evidence package.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit all serving-runtime data-plane images for cryptographic library usage, producing a per-image module inventory that classifies each linked crypto library as validated or non-validated and identifies request-path usage.\n38\t- Remediate every data-plane image so that the request path uses only validated cryptographic modules on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters (rebuilds, library replacements, or base-image changes as the audit dictates — the remediation mechanism per image is an implementation decision for the team).\n39\t- Verify correct serving behavior (inference request path) for the remediated runtime images on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters, in the deployment modes the stack supports.\n40\t- Author and verify the FIPS regression gating CI check covering the data-plane images: a gating check that fails any serving-runtime build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. This epic owns the portion of the stack-wide FIPS regression enforcement (HLR-3) that covers the serving-runtime surface.\n41\t- Produce build attestations for every remediated data-plane image and hand off the per-image module inventory, attestations, and FIPS test results as inputs to the compliance evidence package.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A module inventory exists for every serving-runtime data-plane image, classifying each linked cryptographic library as validated or non-validated and recording request-path usage.\n46\t- Every remediated data-plane image runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with no non-validated crypto in the inference request path, demonstrated by test results captured per image.\n47\t- The FIPS regression gating check fails a serving-runtime build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes a clean build (verified with a deliberate negative test), and it is wired as a gating check in the serving-runtime build pipelines.\n48\t- Build attestations are produced for every remediated data-plane image and are available to the compliance evidence package.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — serving data-plane portion (\"all serving-stack images\"): the model-execution runtime images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules.\n53\t- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — this epic authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check covering the data-plane images it remediates; the check spans exactly the same images and build pipelines as the remediation, so it is not separately schedulable from this epic.\n54\t- **HLR-2 (P0, partial input)** — produces the data-plane module inventory, build attestations, and test results consumed by the compliance evidence package.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8c4ca52e959c858","agent_id":"a0d11201cf9072289","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"e27a9f62-740b-431a-b42c-e6d7f970e317","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:27:24.092Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-895919f770e60d9b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
