team).\n39\t- Verify correct operator behavior on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n40\t- Author and verify the FIPS regression gating CI check covering the Platform Operator image: a gating check that fails any Platform Operator build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. This epic owns the portion of the stack-wide FIPS regression enforcement (HLR-3) that covers the Platform Operator surface.\n41\t- Produce build attestations for the remediated operator image and hand off the module inventory, attestations, and FIPS test results as inputs to the compliance evidence package.\n42\t\n43\t## Risks / Notes\n44\t\n45\t- The Platform Operator has no architecture-context file in `.context/architecture-context/`; its build and attestation pipeline posture could not be corroborated during decomposition. Confirm the operator's build pipeline can produce the attestations the evidence package requires before scheduling.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A module inventory exists for the Platform Operator image, classifying each linked cryptographic library as validated or non-validated and recording request-path usage.\n50\t- The remediated Platform Operator image runs correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster with no non-validated crypto in the request path, demonstrated by captured test results.\n51\t- The FIPS regression gating check fails a Platform Operator build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage and passes a clean build (verified with a deliberate negative test), and it is wired as a gating check in the operator's build pipeline.\n52\t- Build attestations are produced for the remediated operator image and are available to the compliance evidence package.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — Platform Operator portion (\"all serving-stack images\"): the operator image runs correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules.\n57\t- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)** — this epic authors and verifies the FIPS regression gating check covering the Platform Operator image it remediates; the check spans exactly the same image and build pipeline as the remediation, so it is not separately schedulable from this epic.\n58\t- **HLR-2 (P0, partial input)** — produces the operator module inventory, build attestations, and test results consumed by the compliance evidence package.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a33364966471fe34","agent_id":"af492226073e666b9","session_id":"c8475876-08d1-4b69-838f-3e562b4843af","uuid":"720c6a77-61f7-437b-bfb6-5f19120428ee","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:28:34.067Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-949ee0bae569d112","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013"}
